++Email application++

```
apps/emails/js/emails.js
```

This application implements typical features associated with email functionality,
such as initialization, server actions, email deletion, sending, setting states,
handling signatures, generating and downloading PDFs, viewing email sources, replying
and forwarding.


+++Main object+++

```
saltos.emails = {};
```

This object contains all SaltOS code related to email operations.


+++Initialize the email application+++

```
saltos.emails.init = arg
```

This method handles initialization tasks for different views (`create`, `view`, `close`, `list`)
in the email application. It manages UI updates, visibility behaviors, and email state changes.

- @param {string} arg Specifies the type of view or action to initialize.


+++Load folders+++

```
saltos.emails.folders = ()
```

This method loads the tree of folders of the accounts of the user, marking as selected
the node of the account and the folder of the search form


+++Folders select helper+++

```
saltos.emails.__folders_select = (nodes, id)
```

This method marks as selected the node of the tree that matches the id, and opens it and
its parents to show it and its children when it is inside a closed node or when it is a
closed node, like the disabled accounts

- @nodes => the nodes of the tree
- @id    => the id of the node to select


Returns true if the node is found


+++Select folder+++

```
saltos.emails.folder = value
```

This method is executed when a node of the tree is selected, the value contains the
account and the folder separated by a slash (folder 0 for all folders of the account),
sets both in the search form and searchs the emails


+++All emails+++

```
saltos.emails.folder_all = ()
```

This method shows the emails of all the accounts together in the same list (except the
trash and the junk), keeping the other filters of the search form, and reloads the
folders tree to remove the selection of the previous folder


+++Reset filter+++

```
saltos.emails.reset = ()
```

This method resets the search filter and reloads the folders tree to remove the
selection of the previous folder


+++Folders data+++

```
saltos.emails.__folders_data = [];
```

This property stores the last data loaded in the folders tree


+++Selected folder helper+++

```
saltos.emails.__folder_selected = ()
```

This method returns the account and the folder selected in the tree, and the nodes of
both, or shows a modal and returns null if no account is selected


+++Folder action helper+++

```
saltos.emails.__folder_action = data
```

This method sends an action of the folders management to the server, shows the response,
reloads the folders tree and updates the list of emails

- @data => the data of the action


+++Folders panel+++

```
saltos.emails.folders_panel = ()
```

This method shows and hides the folders panel, an offcanvas with the folders tree and its
options, using the same mechanism of the search form (saltos.common.filter): the
contents of the folders_panel div are moved to the offcanvas while it is open


+++Folder modal helper+++

```
saltos.emails.__folder_modal = ()
```

This method programs the close of the modal of the folders management when the search
form, that contains the folders tree, is closed


+++Create folder+++

```
saltos.emails.folder_create = ()
```

This method shows a modal to create a new folder in the account selected in the tree,
using the selected folder as default parent


+++Server folders+++

```
saltos.emails.folder_server = ()
```

This method shows a modal with the folders of the server of the IMAP account selected in
the tree, to subscribe and unsubscribe them: the emails of the subscribed folders are
synchronized, and the emails of the unsubscribed folders are deleted in SaltOS (they stay
in the server); the special folders can not be changed


+++Rename folder+++

```
saltos.emails.folder_rename = ()
```

This method shows a modal to rename the folder selected in the tree


+++Move folder+++

```
saltos.emails.folder_move = ()
```

This method shows a modal to move the folder selected in the tree inside another folder
of the same account


+++Delete folder+++

```
saltos.emails.folder_delete = ()
```

This method shows a modal with the summary of the folders and emails affected and
deletes the folder selected in the tree with its subfolders, the emails are moved
to the trash, and the emails of the account are shown after the delete


+++Empty folder+++

```
saltos.emails.folder_empty = folder
```

This method shows a modal with the number of emails affected and deletes permanently
the emails of the trash or the junk folder of the account selected in the tree

- @folder => the folder to empty, trash or junk


+++Move selected emails+++

```
saltos.emails.move1 = ()
```

This method moves the emails selected in the list to another folder


+++Move this email+++

```
saltos.emails.move2 = ()
```

This method moves the email opened in the view to another folder


+++Move helper+++

```
saltos.emails.__move = ids
```

This method shows a modal with the folders of the account of the emails, and moves the
emails to the selected folder, all emails must be of the same account

- @ids => the ids of the emails separated by commas


+++Move rows helper+++

```
saltos.emails.__move_rows = (nodes, rows, prefix, skip = '')
```

This method converts the nodes of the folders of an account in the rows of a select,
using the path of each folder as label

- @nodes  => the nodes of the tree
- @rows   => the array where the rows are added
- @prefix => the path of the parent node
- @skip   => the id of the node excluded with its children (optional)


+++Perform server-related actions for emails+++

```
saltos.emails.server = ()
```

This method triggers server-side actions for emails and displays the responses in toasts,
then updates the list and the folders tree (the synchronization can change the folders).


+++Delete selected emails+++

```
saltos.emails.delete1 = ()
```

This method deletes multiple emails selected by the user, after showing a confirmation modal.


+++Delete a single email+++

```
saltos.emails.delete2 = ()
```

This method deletes the currently viewed email after showing a confirmation modal.


+++Send an email+++

```
saltos.emails.send = ()
```

This method validates the required fields and sends the email data to the server.
It handles responses and clears unsaved data on success.


+++Set email state+++

```
saltos.emails.setter = what
```

This function updates the state of a specific email identified by its ID. The updated state is sent
to the server, and the UI is refreshed afterward.

- @param {string} what Specifies the state to set for the email.


+++Add signature to email+++

```
saltos.emails.signature = ()
```

This function applies the email signature based on the selected account and its related data.
The signature is retrieved from the server and updated in the email form.


+++View email source+++

```
saltos.emails.source = ()
```

This function opens the raw source of the selected email for viewing in the driver.


+++Reply to an email+++

```
saltos.emails.reply = ()
```

This function opens the reply form for the currently selected email.


+++Reply to all recipients of an email+++

```
saltos.emails.replyall = ()
```

This function opens the reply-all form for the currently selected email, including all recipients.


+++Forward an email+++

```
saltos.emails.forward = ()
```

This function opens the forward form for the currently selected email.


+++Driver search+++

```
saltos.driver.search = arg
```

This function implement the search feature associated to tables and lists
using the filters fields

Additionally, translates the `body_text` field of each result
before rendering the list.

- @arg => unused at this scope


++Emails accounts library++

```
apps/emails/php/accounts.php
```

This library contains the functions used by the emails accounts app


+++Used libraries+++

```
use PHPMailer\PHPMailer\PHPMailer;
```

This use loads the external libraries needed to run this library.


+++Test the connection of an account+++

```
function emails_accounts_test($json)
```

This function tests the incoming server (POP3 or IMAP) or the outgoing server (SMTP),
according to the server field, using the data of the account form, without saving it

- @json => the data of the account form, with the server to test, incoming or outgoing


Returns an array with the status, ok or error, and the message


+++Test the incoming server+++

```
function emails_accounts_test_incoming($value)
```

This function connects and logins with the incoming server and reports the number of
emails (POP3) or the number of folders (IMAP)

- @value => the function used to get the fields of the account form


Returns an array with the status, ok or error, and the message


+++Test the outgoing server+++

```
function emails_accounts_test_outgoing($value)
```

This function connects and authenticates with the SMTP server using PHPMailer, the
local servers (mail, sendmail and qmail) are not tested

- @value => the function used to get the fields of the account form


Returns an array with the status, ok or error, and the message


++Email Query Builder++

```
apps/emails/php/filter.php
```

This function builds an SQL WHERE query for filtering emails based on various criteria
such as account, fields, search terms, dates, and specific email states.


+++Generate WHERE query for emails+++

```
function make_where_query_emails($json)
```

This function takes a JSON input and generates a dynamic SQL WHERE clause to filter emails.
The query is constructed based on several optional parameters such as account ID, search fields,
dates, and flags indicating specific states (e.g., new emails, waiting emails).

- @json => Input parameters for generating the query.


Returns the dynamically constructed SQL WHERE clause.


++Emails folders++

```
apps/emails/php/folders.php
```

This file contains the functions used to manage the folders of the emails accounts


+++Check the folders of an account+++

```
function emails_folders_check($account_id)
```

This function checks the folders of the account, creating the mandatory folders (inbox,
sent, trash and junk) of the POP3 accounts when they not exists; too removes the folders
of the deleted accounts

- @account_id => the id of the account


Returns an array with the ids of the mandatory folders indexed by special use, or an
empty array if the account not exists


+++Insert an account+++

```
function emails_accounts_insert($json)
```

This function inserts a new emails account using the generic insert action and creates
the mandatory folders of the new account

- @json => the data of the new account


Returns the result of the insert action


+++Folders tree+++

```
function emails_folders_tree($ids = '')
```

This function returns the tree of folders of the accounts of the current user, using the
format of the jstree widget: one node for each account with its folders as children, the
id of each node contains the account and the folder separated by a slash, using the
folder 0 for the nodes of the accounts, the enabled accounts are shown first and opened,
and the disabled accounts are shown at the end and closed

- @ids => the ids of the emails used to limit the tree to its accounts (optional)


Returns an array with the nodes of the tree


+++Folders tree helper+++

```
function __emails_folders_tree_helper($account_id, $folders, $parent_id)
```

This function returns the nodes of the folders that are children of the parent folder,
the names of the special folders are translated

- @account_id => the id of the account
- @folders    => the array with all folders of the account
- @parent_id  => the id of the parent folder


Returns an array with the nodes of the children folders


+++Move emails to a folder+++

```
function __emails_folders_move($ids, $special_use)
```

This function moves the emails to the folder of its account identified by the special
use, it is an internal helper that not checks the permissions, the callers must check
that the emails are of the current user; the moves of the emails of the IMAP accounts
are enqueued, and the emails of the IMAP accounts without that folder are not moved

- @ids         => the ids of the emails separated by commas
- @special_use => the special use of the destination folder


+++Move emails to a folder by id+++

```
function emails_folders_move_to($ids, $folder_id)
```

This function moves the emails to the folder identified by its id, the folder must be of
an account of the current user and only the emails of the same account are moved

- @ids       => the ids of the emails separated by commas
- @folder_id => the id of the destination folder


Returns a response message with the number of moved emails


+++Folders action+++

```
function emails_folders_action($json)
```

This function executes the actions of the folders management requested by the client

- @json => the data of the request: action, account_id, folder_id, parent_id, label and
         folder (trash or junk, used to empty these folders)


Returns a response message


+++Folders get helper+++

```
function __emails_folders_get($folder_id)
```

This function returns the folder if it is a folder of an account of the current user

- @folder_id => the id of the folder


Returns an array with the fields of the folder or null if not found


+++Folders IMAP helper+++

```
function __emails_folders_imap($account_id)
```

This function checks if the account is an IMAP account, whose folders are managed in
the server

- @account_id => the id of the account


Returns true if the account is an IMAP account


+++Folders exists helper+++

```
function __emails_folders_exists($account_id, $parent_id, $label, $folder_id = 0)
```

This function checks if exists a folder with the same label in the same parent

- @account_id => the id of the account
- @parent_id  => the id of the parent folder
- @label      => the label of the folder
- @folder_id  => the id of the folder excluded from the check


Returns true if exists another folder with the same label


+++Folders create helper+++

```
function __emails_folders_create($account_id, $parent_id, $label)
```

This function creates a new folder in the account, inside the parent folder

- @account_id => the id of the account
- @parent_id  => the id of the parent folder, 0 for the root
- @label      => the label of the new folder


Returns a response message


+++Folders rename helper+++

```
function __emails_folders_rename($folder_id, $label)
```

This function renames a folder, the special folders can not be renamed

- @folder_id => the id of the folder
- @label     => the new label of the folder


Returns a response message


+++Folders tree ids helper+++

```
function __emails_folders_tree_ids($account_id, $folder_id)
```

This function returns the id of the folder and the ids of all its subfolders

- @account_id => the id of the account
- @folder_id  => the id of the folder


Returns an array with the ids


+++Folders move helper+++

```
function __emails_folders_move_parent($folder_id, $parent_id)
```

This function moves a folder and its subfolders inside another folder of the same
account, the special folders can not be moved

- @folder_id => the id of the folder
- @parent_id => the id of the new parent folder, 0 for the root


Returns a response message


+++Folders summary+++

```
function emails_folders_summary($json)
```

This function returns the message used to confirm the delete of a folder, with the
number of subfolders and emails affected, or the error if the folder can not be deleted

- @json => the data of the request, with the folder_id


Returns an array with the status (ok or ko) and the message


+++Folders delete helper+++

```
function __emails_folders_delete($folder_id)
```

This function deletes a folder and its subfolders, moving its emails to the trash of
the account, the special folders can not be deleted

- @folder_id => the id of the folder


Returns a response message


+++Folders empty ids helper+++

```
function __emails_folders_empty_ids($account_id, $special_use)
```

This function returns the ids of the emails of the special folder of the account, the
account must be of the current user

- @account_id  => the id of the account
- @special_use => the special use of the folder


Returns an array with the ids of the emails, or null if the account is not of the user


+++Folders empty summary+++

```
function emails_folders_empty_summary($json)
```

This function returns the message used to confirm the empty of the trash or the junk
folder of the account, with the number of emails affected, or the error if the folder
can not be emptied (also when it is already empty)

- @json => the data of the request, with the account_id and the folder (trash or junk)


Returns an array with the status (ok or ko) and the message


+++Folders empty helper+++

```
function __emails_folders_empty($account_id, $special_use)
```

This function deletes permanently the emails of the trash or the junk folder of the
account, the emails of the junk are moved to the trash before to be deleted because
the delete action only removes permanently the emails that are in the trash

- @account_id  => the id of the account
- @special_use => the special use of the folder


Returns a response message


+++Folders of the server+++

```
function emails_folders_server($json)
```

This function returns the folders of an IMAP account of the current user, refreshed from
the server, used by the dialog to subscribe and unsubscribe the folders: the special
folders and the folders that can not contain emails can not be changed

- @json => the data of the request, with the account_id


Returns an array with the status and the folders (name, subscribed and locked), or with
the status and the error message


+++Folders subscribe helper+++

```
function __emails_folders_subscribe($account_id, $ids)
```

This function sets the folders subscribed of an IMAP account: the folders of the list
not subscribed are subscribed and the folders not in the list subscribed are
unsubscribed (deleting its emails in SaltOS), except the special folders and the folders
that can not contain emails

- @account_id => the id of the account
- @ids        => the ids of the folders that must be subscribed, separated by commas


Returns a response message


++Get email library++

```
apps/emails/php/getmail.php
```

This library provides the necesary functions to download, parse and manage emails.


+++Requires section+++

```
require_once 'apps/emails/php/mailparse.php';
```

This requires loads the external libraries needed to run this library.


+++Defines section+++

```
// phpcs:disable Generic.Files.LineLength
```

This defines allow to define some useful standards to do html pages and more.


+++Remove all body+++

```
function __getmail_removebody($array)
```

This function removes the body entry in the array, it is only for debug purposes

- @aarray => The array that you want to process


+++Process message+++

```
function __getmail_processmessage($disp, $type)
```

This function returns a boolean that identify if the disposition and the type
allow the node to be processed.

- @disp => disposition, can be inline or attachment
- @type => type, can be message, html or plain


+++Process plain html+++

```
function __getmail_processplainhtml($disp, $type)
```

This function returns a boolean that identify if the disposition and the type
allow the node to be processed.

- @disp => disposition, can be inline or attachment
- @type => type, can be message, html or plain


+++Process file+++

```
function __getmail_processfile($disp, $type)
```

This function returns a boolean that identify if the disposition and the type
allow the node to be processed.

- @disp => disposition, can be inline or attachment
- @type => type, can be message, html or plain


+++Check permissions+++

```
function __getmail_checkperm($id)
```

This function allow to check if the current user has permissions to view the
message identified by the id argument

- @id => id of the email


+++Get GZ File+++

```
function __getmail_gzfile($id)
```

This function returns the file that contains the email

- @id => id of the email


+++Get source+++

```
function __getmail_getsource($id)
```

This function returns the original RFC822 message as string

- @id => id of the email


Notes:

This function returns the email source without the base64 attachments


+++Mime decode protected+++

```
function __getmail_mime_decode_protected($input)
```

This function decodes the input string that contains the RFC822 message
using the mime_parser_class to do it, and returns the decoded array.

- @input => the RFC822 string that contains the message


+++Get mime+++

```
function __getmail_getmime($id)
```

This function returns the decoded array of the email identified by the id
argument, to do this more optimal, this function uses an internal cache
file to improve the performance for repeated executions.

- @id => id of the email


+++Get Node+++

```
function __getmail_getnode($path, $array)
```

This function returns the node using a xpath notation

- @path  => xpath that identify the desired path that must to be returned
- @array => the decoded message in an array format


+++Get type+++

```
function __getmail_gettype($array)
```

This function tries to unify the differents content-type to standarize it into
the follow formats: html, plain, messsage, alternative, multipart or other.

- @array => the decoded message in an array format


+++Get disposition+++

```
function __getmail_getdisposition($array)
```

This function tries to unify the differents content-dispoaition to standarize
it into the follow formats: attachment, inline or other.

- @array => the decoded message in an array format


+++Get files+++

```
function __getmail_getfiles($array, $level = 0)
```

This function returns an array with the attachment files of the message

- @array => the decoded message in an array format
- @level => this parameter is internally used to detect recursion


+++Get info+++

```
function __getmail_getinfo($array)
```

Returns all information of the decoded message in a structured format

- @array => the decoded message in an array format


+++Fix string+++

```
function __getmail_fixstring($arg)
```

This function is a helper used by all functions that pcoesses the headers
of the decoded message.

- @arg => the string that must to be checked and fixed if needed


+++Get text body+++

```
function __getmail_gettextbody($array, $level = 0)
```

This function returns all text body concatenated as an unique string

- @array => the decoded message in an array format
- @level => this parameter is internally used to detect recursion


+++Get full body+++

```
function __getmail_getfullbody($array)
```

This function returns all body and attachments information as an array

- @array => the decoded message in an array format


+++Get cid+++

```
function __getmail_getcid($array, $hash)
```

This function returns the requested attachment indentified by the hash argument

- @array => the decoded message in an array format
- @hash  => the hash of the content requested


+++Insert+++

```
function __getmail_insert($file, $messageid, $fields = [])
```

This function does the insert of an email in the app_emails table, with its addresses,
its attachments, its control register and its index

- @file      => the gzfile that contains the message in RFC822 format
- @messageid => the id of the message (account_id/uidl)
- @fields    => the fields of the app_emails table that replace the default values and the
              values computed from the message (optional), like:
              state_new (default 1), state_reply, state_forward, state_wait, email_id (the
              id of the related email), is_outbox, state_sent, state_error (default 0 or
              empty), folder_id (default the inbox, the sent for the outbox and the junk
              for the spam, if they exist) and the IMAP fields imap_uid, imap_messageid
              and imap_emailid


+++Update+++

```
function __getmail_update($field, $value, $id)
```

This function updates the field with the value of the app_emails for the
register identified by the id argument.

- @field => field that you want to update
- @value => value that you want to set
- @id    => id of the register to do the update


+++Add bcc+++

```
function __getmail_add_bcc($id, $bcc)
```

This function adds the bbc to the database, this is because the messages
does not contains the bcc field (is hidden in theory), and only is available
if the current execution is the sender of the message.

- @id  => id of the email
- @bcc => an array with the addresses of the emails


+++Gzfile size+++

```
function gzfilesize($filename)
```

This function is copied from http://php.net/manual/es/function.gzread.php#110078
and allow to know the file size of the file after a gzip descompression.

- @filename => the gzip filename that you want to know the size


+++Get email body+++

```
function getmail_body($id, $images = false)
```

This function returns the string that contains the body of the email
intended to be rendered in an iframe, for example

- @id => id of the email


+++Generate formatted email header information+++

```
function __getmail_head_helper($decoded, $email_id)
```

This function extracts and formats header details from the decoded email structure,
including sender, recipients, date, subject, and attachments. It handles edge cases
such as missing data, and ensures that all information is presented in a structured
and readable format. HTML encoding is applied to ensure safe display within a web interface.

- @decoded  => Decoded structure of the email, containing metadata and header information.
- @email_id => ID of the email to retrieve additional account-specific details.


Returns a formatted HTML string with the email header information.


+++Extract and format the body of an email+++

```
function __getmail_body_helper($decoded, $images = false)
```

This function processes the decoded content of an email, extracting the plain
text and HTML bodies while applying necessary transformations for safe and
structured display. It handles inline images, styles, and embedded attachments,
ensuring compatibility and security.

- @decoded => Decoded structure of the email, typically containing nodes with
            metadata and body content.
- @images  => Specifies whether inline images should be embedded directly into
            the content.


Returns the formatted email body, including plain text, HTML, and inline attachments.


+++Get email source+++

```
function getmail_source($id)
```

This function returns the string that contains the source of the email
intended to be rendered in an iframe, for example

- @id => id of the email


+++Get email files+++

```
function getmail_files($id)
```

This function returns an arryy that contains the files of the email
intended to be rendered in an table, for example

- @id => id of the email


+++Get cid+++

```
function getmail_cid($id, $cid)
```

This function returns the requested attachment indentified by the cid argument

- @id  => id of the email
- @cid => the cid of the content requested


+++Is outbox+++

```
function getmail_field($field, $id)
```

Returns the field of the email identified by the id argument

- @field => field requested
- @id    => id of the email


+++Server+++

```
function getmail_server()
```

This function implements the old getmail action of the old saltos.


+++Folders hash+++

```
function __getmail_folders_hash()
```

This function returns a hash of the folders of the accounts of the current user, with
the fields shown in the folders tree, used to detect the changes of the folders done by
the synchronization of the IMAP accounts

Returns the hash of the folders


+++Delete+++

```
function getmail_delete($ids)
```

This function implements the old delete action of the old saltos.

- @ids => array with the emails id


+++Delete helper+++

```
function __getmail_delete($ids)
```

This function deletes permanently the emails, its files, its addresses, its attachments
and its control and index registers, without permission checks (the callers must check
them), for the emails of all the protocols

- @ids => the ids of the emails separated by commas


+++Get viewpdf+++

```
function getmail_viewpdf($id, $cid)
```

This function returns the requested attachment indentified by the cid argument
in a pdf format for the viewpdf widget

- @id  => id of the email
- @cid => the cid of the content requested


+++Get download+++

```
function getmail_download($id, $cid)
```

This function returns the requested attachment indentified by the cid argument
in an array format for the download feature

- @id  => id of the email
- @cid => the cid of the content requested


+++Update email states+++

```
function getmail_setter($ids, $what)
```

This function modifies the state of emails (e.g., `new` or `wait`)
based on the provided IDs and action. It validates user permissions for the
selected emails before updating their states. The function calculates the
number of records to be modified and updates the database accordingly.

- @ids  => Comma-separated list of email IDs to be updated.
- @what => Specifies the state change in the format `key=value` (e.g., `new=0`).


Returns a response message indicating the number of emails modified.


+++Generate PDF from emails+++

```
function getmail_pdf($ids)
```

This function generates PDF files for the provided email IDs using either the
`chromium` command or a fallback library. If multiple emails are selected,
their PDFs are merged into a single file. It validates user permissions for
accessing the emails and manages caching for performance optimization.

- @ids => List or comma-separated string of email IDs to generate PDFs for.


Returns metadata of the generated PDF file, including its name, type, and
base64-encoded data.


+++Generate iframe content with secure policies+++

```
function __iframe_srcdoc_helper($html)
```

This function generates the `srcdoc` content for an iframe element, embedding
the provided HTML string. It ensures the content is styled using predefined
fonts and enforces a strict Content Security Policy (CSP) to limit the sources
for styles, fonts, and images. This helps maintain security and compatibility
within the iframe.

- @html => The HTML content to be embedded in the iframe.


Return a complete HTML document string suitable for `srcdoc` use in an iframe.


++Get email IMAP library++

```
apps/emails/php/getmail_imap.php
```

This library contains the functions used to synchronize the IMAP accounts with the
server: the folders, the emails and its flags


+++Synchronize an account+++

```
function getmail_imap($account, &$newemail)
```

This function connects with the IMAP server of the account, applies the pending
operations of the queue and synchronizes the folders and the emails of the subscribed
folders

- @account  => the row of the account
- @newemail => the counter of the new emails, incremented with the downloaded emails


Returns an empty string on success or the error message


+++IMAP client+++

```
function __getmail_imap_client($account): imap_class
```

This function returns the IMAP client configured with the incoming server of the
account, not connected

- @account => the row of the account


Returns the IMAP client


+++Synchronize the folders+++

```
function __getmail_imap_folders($imap, $account_id)
```

This function updates the folders of the account with the folders of the server: adds the
new folders, updates the existing ones and removes the folders that not exists in the
server, the folders are identified by its full name; the sent, the trash and the junk
are created in the server if they not exist; the inbox, the sent, the trash, the junk
and the archive are always subscribed; in the first synchronization of the account,
the folders subscribed in the server are subscribed too, the rest of the folders are
subscribed by the user

- @imap       => the IMAP client connected with the server
- @account_id => the id of the account


Returns an empty string on success or the error message


+++Special folders+++

```
function __getmail_imap_specials($imap, $folders)
```

This function completes the folders of the server with the sent, the trash and the junk
folders used by SaltOS: if there is no folder with the special use, a root folder with
the standard name (Sent, Trash or Junk) is used as the special folder, otherwise it is
created and subscribed in the server (with its special use if the server supports
CREATE-SPECIAL-USE); the folders that the server does not create are retried in the next
synchronization

- @imap    => the IMAP client connected with the server
- @folders => the folders returned by the ListFolders of the IMAP client


Returns the folders with the special folders, or the error message if the connection fails


+++Depth of a folder+++

```
function __getmail_imap_depth($folder)
```

This function returns the number of levels of the full name of the folder, used to sort
the folders with the parents before its children

- @folder => the folder returned by the ListFolders of the IMAP client


Returns the number of delimiters found in the full name


+++Synchronize the emails+++

```
function __getmail_imap_emails($imap, $account_id, &$newemail)
```

This function synchronizes the emails of the subscribed folders in three steps: first
finds the vanished emails (in SaltOS but not in the server) and the appeared emails (in
the server but not in SaltOS) of all the folders, then matches them in all the account to
detect the emails moved by other clients, and the emails without UID with the appeared
emails of its folder, and finally deletes the vanished emails not matched and downloads
the appeared emails not matched; the emails with pending operations in the queue are
frozen: they are never vanished and its flags are not changed

- @imap       => the IMAP client connected with the server
- @account_id => the id of the account
- @newemail   => the counter of the new emails, incremented with the downloaded emails


Returns an empty string on success or the error message


+++Find the vanished and the appeared emails+++

```
function __getmail_imap_scan($imap, $account_id, $frozen, &$vanished, &$appeared)
```

This function compares the UIDs of the subscribed folders in the server with the UIDs of
the emails in SaltOS: the emails of a folder with a new UIDVALIDITY and the emails of
the folders removed in the server are vanished too, except the frozen emails; the UIDs of
the pending operations are known, so the emails moved in SaltOS and not yet in the server
do not appear in its old folder; the folders without changes since the last
synchronization (same UIDVALIDITY, same UIDNEXT and the same number of emails) are not
searched; too synchronizes the flags of the emails of each folder, except the frozen
emails, and the state of each folder is saved for the next synchronization

- @imap       => the IMAP client connected with the server
- @account_id => the id of the account
- @frozen     => the ids of the emails with pending operations as keys
- @vanished   => filled with the ids of the vanished emails
- @appeared   => filled with the UIDs of the appeared emails by folder id


Returns an empty string on success or the error message


+++Match the vanished and the appeared emails+++

```
function __getmail_imap_match($imap, $frozen, &$vanished, $orphans, &$appeared)
```

This function matches one to one the appeared emails with the vanished emails of the
account, to detect the emails moved by other clients (or the emails of a folder with a
new UIDVALIDITY), and with the emails without UID of the same folder (moved in SaltOS
without learning its new UID): first by the Email-ID (OBJECTID or Gmail) and then by the
Message-ID and the size; the ambiguous cases (more than one candidate) are not matched,
so the vanished emails are deleted and the appeared emails are downloaded; the matched
emails get its folder, its UID and the states of its flags (except the frozen emails),
the UIDs learned are written in its pending operations, and the matched emails are
removed from the vanished and the appeared emails

- @imap     => the IMAP client connected with the server
- @frozen   => the ids of the emails with pending operations as keys
- @vanished => the ids of the vanished emails
- @orphans  => the emails without UID in a folder of the account
- @appeared => the UIDs of the appeared emails by folder id


Returns an empty string on success or the error message


+++Download the appeared emails+++

```
function __getmail_imap_download($imap, $account_id, $appeared, &$newemail)
```

This function downloads the appeared emails, the newest first of each folder and up to
the batch size of the config, the rest are downloaded in the next synchronizations

- @imap       => the IMAP client connected with the server
- @account_id => the id of the account
- @appeared   => the UIDs of the appeared emails by folder id
- @newemail   => the counter of the new emails, incremented with the downloaded emails


Returns an empty string on success or the error message


+++Download an email+++

```
function __getmail_imap_message($imap, $account_id, $folder_id, $uid)
```

This function downloads an email of the selected folder, stores it in the inbox directory
of the account using a new uidl generated by SaltOS, that never changes, and inserts it
with its folder, its UID, its Message-ID, its Email-ID (OBJECTID or Gmail) and the states
of its flags

- @imap       => the IMAP client connected with the server
- @account_id => the id of the account
- @folder_id  => the id of the selected folder
- @uid        => the UID of the email in the selected folder


Returns an empty string on success or the error message


+++Email-ID item+++

```
function __getmail_imap_emailid_item($imap)
```

This function returns the item of the FETCH command used to get the Email-ID of the
emails, a stable id that not changes when the email is moved: EMAILID (OBJECTID) or
X-GM-MSGID (Gmail), or an empty string if the server not supports any of them

- @imap => the IMAP client connected with the server


Returns the item with a leading space or an empty string


+++Message-ID and Email-ID+++

```
function __getmail_imap_ids($data)
```

This function returns the Message-ID (from the header returned by the FETCH command,
unfolding the header lines) and the Email-ID (EMAILID or X-GM-MSGID) of an email

- @data => the items of the email returned by the FETCH command


Returns an array with the Message-ID and the Email-ID, empty strings if not found


+++Synchronize the flags+++

```
function __getmail_imap_flags($imap, $folder, $state, $local)
```

This function updates the states of the emails of the selected folder with its flags in
the server, that wins: with CONDSTORE only the emails changed since the HIGHESTMODSEQ of
the last synchronization (nothing if it is the same), otherwise all the emails

- @imap   => the IMAP client connected with the server
- @folder => the row of the selected folder, with the HIGHESTMODSEQ of the last
           synchronization
- @state  => the state of the selected folder returned by the SELECT command
- @local  => the ids of the emails of the folder in SaltOS by UID


Returns an empty string on success or the error message


+++States of the flags+++

```
function __getmail_imap_states($data)
```

This function returns the states of an email from its flags: state_new is not \Seen,
state_reply is \Answered, state_forward is $Forwarded and state_wait is \Flagged

- @data => the items of the email returned by the FETCH command, with the FLAGS item


Returns an array with the states


+++Enqueue an operation+++

```
function __getmail_imap_enqueue($email_id, $action, $fields = [])
```

This function adds an operation done in SaltOS to the queue of the account of the email,
to be applied in the server by the next synchronization: the operation acts on the email
in the folder where it is now in SaltOS, with its UID if known, or without UID (0) if it
depends on a pending move of the same email; the operations on emails that never were in
the server (without UID and without pending operations) are not enqueued, except the
append, that puts them in the server; the UIDs 0 and
NULL mean unknown UID, because the IMAP UIDs start at 1 and the insert and update helpers
store the NULL values of the integer fields as 0

- @email_id => the id of the email
- @action   => the operation: flag_add, flag_remove, move, expunge or append
- @fields   => the other fields of the operation: flag (flag_add and flag_remove) or
             to_folder_id (move and append)


Returns true if the operation is enqueued, false otherwise


+++Enqueue a change of state+++

```
function __getmail_imap_state($ids, $field, $value)
```

This function enqueues the flag of a change of state of the emails of the IMAP accounts
that change: state_new is \Seen (inverted), state_wait is \Flagged, state_reply is
\Answered and state_forward is $Forwarded; it must be called before the change is done
in SaltOS, it is an internal helper that not checks the permissions

- @ids   => the ids of the emails, separated by commas or as array
- @field => the state that changes
- @value => the new value of the state, 0 or 1


+++Enqueue a move+++

```
function __getmail_imap_move($ids, $folder_id)
```

This function enqueues the move of the emails of the IMAP accounts to another folder of
its account, and sets its UID as unknown (the UID in the destination folder is learned
when the move is applied); it must be called before the folder of the emails is changed
in SaltOS, it is an internal helper that not checks the permissions

- @ids       => the ids of the emails, separated by commas or as array
- @folder_id => the id of the destination folder


+++Enqueue an append+++

```
function __getmail_imap_append($email_id)
```

This function enqueues the append of a sent email of an IMAP account in the sent folder
of the server (the folder of the email in SaltOS), if the copy in the sent folder is
enabled in the account (disabled for the servers that save the copy itself, like Gmail,
whose copy is adopted by the synchronization); it is an internal helper that not checks
the permissions

- @email_id => the id of the email


+++Enqueue an expunge+++

```
function __getmail_imap_expunge($ids)
```

This function enqueues the permanent delete of the emails of the IMAP accounts in the
server; it must be called before the emails are deleted in SaltOS, it is an internal
helper that not checks the permissions

- @ids => the ids of the emails separated by commas


+++Apply the queue+++

```
function __getmail_imap_queue($imap, $account_id)
```

This function applies the pending operations of the account in order: each operation is
removed when done or when the email not exists in the server; the operations without UID
wait until a previous move learns it (or until the synchronization finds it), and after
an error returned by the server the operation is retried in the next synchronization up
to the maximum retries of the config (then it is removed); in both cases the next
operations of the same email wait to keep the order; an error of the connection stops
the synchronization

- @imap       => the IMAP client connected with the server
- @account_id => the id of the account


Returns an empty string on success or the error message of the connection


+++Result of an operation of the queue+++

```
function __getmail_imap_queue_result($imap, $row, $error, &$waiting)
```

This function removes the operation when it is done; after an error returned by the
server, the operation is retried in the next synchronization up to the maximum retries
of the config (then it is removed and logged) and the next operations of the email wait

- @imap    => the IMAP client connected with the server
- @row     => the operation of the queue
- @error   => the result of the operation, empty string on success
- @waiting => the ids of the emails whose operations wait as keys


Returns the error message if it is an error of the connection, otherwise an empty string


+++Append an email of the queue+++

```
function __getmail_imap_queue_append($imap, $row, $names, &$selected)
```

This function puts a sent email in the sent folder of the server: if the email has an
UID it is already in the server (adopted by the synchronization); otherwise the
Message-ID is searched in the folder and, if it is not found, the email is appended with
the \Seen flag; the UID found or returned by the server (UIDPLUS) is learned, otherwise the
next synchronization adopts the email

- @imap     => the IMAP client connected with the server
- @row      => the operation of the queue
- @names    => the full names of the folders of the account by id
- @selected => the full name of the selected folder, updated if the folder is selected


Returns an empty string when done or the error message


+++Move an email of the queue+++

```
function __getmail_imap_queue_move(imap_class $imap, $row, $uid, $to_folder, &$selected)
```

This function moves the email to the destination folder and learns its new UID from
the server (UIDPLUS) or searching its Message-ID in the destination folder when it is
unique; the new UID is written in the next operations of the email up to its next move
(they act on the destination folder), and in the email if there is no next move; if the
new UID is not learned, the next operations wait until the synchronization finds it
matching the email without UID with the appeared emails of the destination folder

- @imap      => the IMAP client connected with the server
- @row       => the operation of the queue
- @uid       => the UID of the email in the selected folder
- @to_folder => the full name of the destination folder
- @selected  => the full name of the selected folder, updated if the destination folder
              is selected to search the Message-ID


Returns an empty string on success or the error message


+++Learn an UID+++

```
function __getmail_imap_learn($email_id, $after, $folder_id, $uid)
```

This function writes the new UID of an email, in a folder, in the pending operations of
the email after an operation (they act on that folder) up to the next move of the email,
and in the email if there is no next move and it is in that folder

- @email_id  => the id of the email
- @after     => the id of the operation that moved the email, 0 to start from the first
- @folder_id => the id of the folder of the new UID
- @uid       => the new UID


+++Full name of a folder+++

```
function __getmail_imap_folder_name($account_id, $parent_id, $label)
```

This function returns the full name in the server (UTF-8) of a folder with the label
inside the parent folder, using the delimiter of the parent folder or, for the root
folders, the delimiter of the INBOX (or of any folder of the account)

- @account_id => the id of the account
- @parent_id  => the id of the parent folder, 0 for the root
- @label      => the label of the folder


Returns an array with the full name and the delimiter


+++Create a folder in the server+++

```
function __getmail_imap_folder_create($account_id, $parent_id, $label)
```

This function creates and subscribes the folder in the server and, if it is done, adds
the folder in SaltOS; it is an internal helper that not checks the permissions

- @account_id => the id of the account
- @parent_id  => the id of the parent folder, 0 for the root
- @label      => the label of the new folder


Returns an empty string on success or the error message


+++Rename or move a folder in the server+++

```
function __getmail_imap_folder_rename($folder, $parent_id, $label)
```

This function renames the folder in the server, with the new label or inside the new
parent folder, and, if it is done, updates the folder and the full names of its
subfolders in SaltOS; it is an internal helper that not checks the permissions

- @folder    => the row of the folder
- @parent_id => the id of the new parent folder, 0 for the root
- @label     => the new label of the folder


Returns an empty string on success or the error message


+++Delete a folder in the server+++

```
function __getmail_imap_folder_delete($folder)
```

This function deletes the folder and its subfolders in the server: first applies the
queue of the account, then moves the emails of each folder to the trash (the emails in
SaltOS get the trash and its new UIDs, or an unknown UID that the next synchronization
learns), and then deletes the folders, the subfolders first; each folder deleted in the
server is deleted in SaltOS; it is an internal helper that not checks the permissions

- @folder => the row of the folder


Returns an empty string on success or the error message


+++Refresh the folders+++

```
function __getmail_imap_folders_refresh($account_id)
```

This function connects with the server and synchronizes the folders of the account,
used by the dialog of the folders of the server; it is an internal helper that not
checks the permissions

- @account_id => the id of the account


Returns an empty string on success or the error message


+++Subscribe and unsubscribe folders+++

```
function __getmail_imap_subscribe($account_id, $subscribe, $unsubscribe)
```

This function subscribes the folders in the server and in SaltOS (its emails are
downloaded by the next synchronizations) and unsubscribes the folders in SaltOS only,
deleting its emails and its pending operations in SaltOS (the emails stay in the server);
it is an internal helper that not checks the permissions

- @account_id  => the id of the account
- @subscribe   => the ids of the folders to subscribe
- @unsubscribe => the ids of the folders to unsubscribe


Returns an empty string on success or the error message


++Get email POP3 library++

```
apps/emails/php/getmail_pop3.php
```

This library contains the functions used to receive the emails of the POP3 accounts


+++Receive an account+++

```
function getmail_pop3($row, &$newemail)
```

This function connects with the POP3 server of the account, downloads the new emails and
removes the expired emails from the server if the delete option of the account is enabled

- @row      => the row of the account
- @newemail => the counter of the new emails, incremented with the downloaded emails


Returns an empty string on success or the error message


+++Delete helper+++

```
function __getmail_pop3_delete($ids)
```

This function stores the uidls of the emails of the POP3 accounts that are deleted in
SaltOS (except the emails of the outbox) in the deletes table, to not download them
again while they are in the server; it must be called before the emails are deleted, it
is an internal helper that not checks the permissions

- @ids => the ids of the emails separated by commas


