- @param     string|null $data   Filled with the bytes read.
- @param-out string    $data
- @return    string              Empty string on success; non-empty error message on failure.


+++Close the connection with the server+++

```
public function Close()
```

- @return string Always returns empty string.


+++Read error helper+++

```
private function ReadError(string $prefix)
```

This function returns the error message of a failed read or write, detecting the
timeouts and the connections closed by the server

- @param  string $prefix The prefix of the error message.
- @return string         The error message.


+Sales+

++Invoices application++

```
apps/sales/js/invoices.js
```

This application provides core functionalities for managing invoices, including creating,
editing, viewing, and exporting invoices in PDF format.


+++Main object+++

```
saltos.invoices = {};
```

This object contains all SaltOS code related to invoice operations.


+++Fix tax dropdown visibility.+++

```
saltos.invoices.onload = instance
```

Reset the parent's overflow property to prevent the tax dropdown
from being clipped or hidden inside the container.


+++Lines columns+++

```
saltos.invoices.cols = {
```

This object defines the position of each column in the lines matrix, the tax and the
withholding columns are always present in the matrix but are hidden when the mode
defined by the company is not by line.


+++Types+++

```
saltos.invoices.types = {
```

This object defines the value used by each type in the taxes master, the modes defined
by the company for each type can be 0 (not used), 1 (one by document) or 2 (by line).


+++Handle and recalculate invoice line totals and tax breakdowns after user edits.+++

```
saltos.invoices.onchange = (instance, cell, x, y, value)
```

This function is triggered after the user modifies any cell in the "lines" matrix
(invoice lines). It performs the following operations:

- Validates and normalizes quantity, price, and discount values:
    - Ensures quantity, price and discount are numeric.
    - Defaults discount to 0 if empty but qty and price are valid.
- Sets the tax and the withholding of the new lines:
    - Uses the value of the document select when the mode is one by document.
    - Uses the value of the default register when the mode is by line.
    - The lines that already have a total are never modified.
- Calculates the line total as: `qty × price × (1 - discount%)`, rounded to 2 decimals.
- Updates the lines grid to reflect computed values.
- Recomputes the taxes matrix:
    - Aggregates taxable bases per type (tax or withholding) and value.
    - Computes the amount for each group: `base × (value% / 100)`.
- Rounds all results to 2 decimals and updates the taxes grid.
- Computes the totals matrix:
    - `subtotal` = sum of all line totals
    - `tax` = sum of all tax amounts
    - `withholding` = sum of all withholding amounts
    - `total` = subtotal + tax - withholding
    - Results are rounded and shown in the totals grid.


- @instance => The spreadsheet instance that triggers the change
- @cell     => The cell that has changed
- @x        => The column of the cell
- @y        => The row of the cell
- @value    => The new value of the cell


+++Apply the tax or the withholding of the document to all lines+++

```
saltos.invoices.onselect = type
```

This function is triggered when the user changes the select used by the one by document
mode, it copies the selected value to all computed lines and recalculates the taxes
and the totals, this allow to use the same structure of data for all modes.

- @type => The type of the select that has changed, can be tax or withholding


++ChartJS widgets for invoices++

```
apps/sales/php/echarts.php
```

This file contains helper functions that generate Chart.js-compatible
datasets for visualizing invoice-related data within SaltOS4.

Each function returns an associative array with 'labels' and 'datasets',
directly usable by `<echarts>` widgets in the XML layout system.

The metrics provided include:
- Daily total invoicing
- Daily average invoice value
- Top 5 customers by total invoiced
- Count of paid vs unpaid invoices
- Average number of days to get paid


All functions rely on data from the `app_invoices` table and assume
only closed invoices (`is_closed = 1`) are relevant.


+++compute_invoice_total_by_day+++

```
function compute_invoice_total_by_day()
```

Computes the total invoiced amount per day, for closed invoices.
Useful for displaying the evolution of total income over time.

Returns a Chart.js-compatible array with labels (dates) and a single dataset (total per day).


+++compute_invoice_avg_by_day+++

```
function compute_invoice_avg_by_day()
```

Computes the average invoice amount per day, considering only closed invoices.
This helps analyze how invoice sizes vary over time.

Returns a Chart.js-compatible array with labels (dates) and a single dataset (average amount).


+++compute_invoice_avg_days_to_pay+++

```
function compute_invoice_avg_days_to_pay()
```

Calculates the average number of days it takes to get paid, based on the difference
between invoice and payment dates, grouped by payment day.

Returns a Chart.js-compatible array: labels (payment dates) and one dataset (average days to pay).


+++compute_top5_customers_by_total+++

```
function compute_top5_customers_by_total()
```

Retrieves the top 5 customers based on total invoiced amount for closed invoices.
Cuts customer names using `intelligence_cut()` for chart readability.

Returns a Chart.js-compatible array: labels (customer names) and one dataset (total invoiced).


+++compute_invoice_paid_vs_pending+++

```
function compute_invoice_paid_vs_pending()
```

Counts how many closed invoices have been paid or are still unpaid.
Produces a pie chart data structure separating "Paid" and "Unpaid".

Returns a Chart.js-compatible array: labels (Paid/Unpaid) and one dataset (count of invoices).


+++compute_invoice_open_vs_closed+++

```
function compute_invoice_open_vs_closed()
```

Counts how many invoices are currently open or closed.
Produces a pie chart data structure separating "Open" and "Closed".

Returns an ECharts-compatible array with one pie series.


++Reverses the process of `make_matrix_data()` for the `invoices` app.++

```
apps/sales/php/invoices.php
```

This function takes a previously generated matrix-style array of invoice data
(grouped as lines, taxes, and totals), compares it with the current values
in the database, and builds a minimal diff-like array that includes only
the fields that have changed, been removed, or added.


+++unmake_matrix_data+++

```
function unmake_matrix_data($json, $invoice_id)
```

Reverse the matrix-encoded invoice data to a diff-style data array.

- @json       => The matrix-encoded invoice data (from make_matrix_data)
- @invoice_id => The invoice ID used to retrieve the original data


Return a diff array representing only the differences between the provided
data and the current state of the database.


+++Get next code+++

```
function get_next_code($table, $field, $prefix)
```

This function returns the next code of a serie, the codes are composed by
a prefix that contains the year and a correlative number, the number is
computed using the numeric value of the codes that begin by the prefix,
by this reason the serie is restarted when the year changes.

- @table  => the table that contains the codes
- @field  => the field that contains the codes
- @prefix => the prefix of the serie, for example PF2026-


+++Generates or completes proforma and final invoice metadata.+++

```
function set_proforma_invoice($json, $invoice_id)
```

This function ensures that the given invoice JSON structure has appropriate values for:
- `proforma_code` and `proforma_date` (if not provided or if it's a new invoice)
- `invoice_code` and `invoice_date` (if the invoice is being closed)
- `is_closed` (based on database if not explicitly set)
- `paid_date` (if the invoice is marked as paid)
- `due_date` (if the invoice is marked as closed)


Rules:
- If no `invoice_id` is given or `proforma_code` is not defined, a new proforma number is generated.
- If the invoice is being closed (`is_closed` is true), a new invoice number is generated.
- If `is_closed` is not defined in the JSON, it's looked up in the database for the given invoice ID.
- If `is_paid` is true and no `paid_date` is set, the current date is assigned.
- If the invoice is closed and no `due_date` is set, the current date is assigned.


- @json       => Invoice data to process and complete.
- @invoice_id => ID of the invoice, used to retrieve current status from DB.


Return the updated JSON with appropriate codes and dates filled in.


++Taxes and withholdings helpers++

```
apps/sales/php/taxes.php
```

This file contains the functions shared by the documents that use taxes and
withholdings in their lines, like the invoices and the quotes, the taxes
and the withholdings are stored in the same master table (app_taxes) and
are differentiated by the type field (0 tax, 1 withholding), and the company
defines how the user operates with each one of them using the tax_mode and
withholding_mode fields (0 not used, 1 one by document, 2 by line).

All functions that request a type as argument expect tax or withholding,
that are the names used as prefix by the fields of each type.


+++Get taxes modes+++

```
function get_taxes_modes()
```

This function returns an array with the mode used by each type, the keys
of the array are tax and withholding and the values can be as follow:

- 0 => the type is not used, nothing is requested to the user
- 1 => the user selects only one value for the entire document
- 2 => the user selects one value for each line of the document


+++Get taxes master+++

```
function get_taxes_master($type = '')
```

This function returns the active registers of the master table, each row
contains the id, name, value, type and default fields.

- @type => the type that you want to retrieve, all types by default


+++Get taxes column+++

```
function get_taxes_column($type, $title)
```

This function returns the definition of the column used by the lines of
the documents, the column is a dropdown with the values of the requested
type when the mode is by line, otherwise the column is hidden, this allow
to use the same structure of data for all modes.

- @type  => the type of the column, can be tax or withholding
- @title => the title of the column


+++Get taxes total column+++

```
function get_taxes_total_column($type, $title)
```

This function returns the definition of the column used by the totals of
the documents, the column is hidden when the type is not used.

- @type  => the type of the column, can be tax or withholding
- @title => the title of the column


+++Get taxes subtotal column+++

```
function get_taxes_subtotal_column($title)
```

This function returns the definition of the subtotal column used by the
totals of the documents, the column is hidden when the taxes and the
withholdings are not used, because the subtotal is the same that the total.

- @title => the title of the column


+++Get taxes rows+++

```
function get_taxes_rows($type)
```

This function returns the rows used by the select of the one by document mode,
the first row is void to allow documents without tax or withholding.

- @type => the type of the rows, can be tax or withholding


+++Get taxes default+++

```
function get_taxes_default($type)
```

This function returns the value of the default register of the requested
type, or a void string if there is not a default register.

- @type => the type of the default, can be tax or withholding


+++Make taxes data+++

```
function make_taxes_data($lines)
```

This function returns the data of the lines used by the documents, the
argument is the list of the lines with the description, quantity, price,
discount, tax_id, tax_value, withholding_id, withholding_value and total
fields, and the returned array contains the matrix of the lines with the
description, quantity, price, discount, tax, withholding and total, and
the values used by the selects of the one by document mode, that only are set
when all lines of the document are using the same value.

- @lines => the list of the lines of the document


+Tester+

++Rating widget example++

```
apps/tester/js/rating.js
```

This file is an example of a widget provided by an application, each widget is registered
in saltos.bootstrap.__field using the name of the type, and since then, it can be used in
the layouts as any other widget of SaltOS, for example, <rating id="xxx"/>.

The data input fields must store in element.saltos the object returned by the helper
saltos.bootstrap.__saltos_helper, and replace the features that need a different behavior,
in this case, the framework (get_data, check_required, form_disabled, form.data and reset)
only uses these features and does not need to know anything about the new widgets.


+++Rating constructor helper+++

```
saltos.bootstrap.__field.rating = field
```

[../code/data/cache/69347ff0e79611abf2a365239c280bb7.png]

This function returns an object of the rating type, it is a data input field that shows
five stars and stores the selected value (from 1 to 5) in a hidden input.

- @id       => the id used by the object
- @class    => allow to add more classes to the stars container
- @value    => the value used as value parameter (from 1 to 5, void or 0 for no stars)
- @disabled => this parameter raise the disabled flag
- @required => this parameter raise the required flag
- @tooltip  => this parameter raise the title flag
- @label    => this parameter is used as text for the label
- @color    => the color of the stars (primary by default)


Notes:

This widget programs all features of the data input fields: set_value paints the stars,
set_disabled disables the buttons of the stars, get_data normalizes the values as integers
and check_required colorizes the stars container and focuses the first star.


